public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterC.Section01.RankTwo.Classification.BinaryCoreBound.MS93.DistanceFour.Early.EdgeStructure.OrderTwo.Generation

/-!
# The two actual conjugate spans in the offender argument

The escaping-neighbor segment can be aligned with the original edge by an
actual stabilizer element. Simultaneous escape (2.1)(vii), using the proved
SL₃(2) conjugate-generation theorem, then shows that the first span leaves
the opposite kernel. A critical pair among its generators puts its central
order-two displacement in the opposite Z-layer as well.

Conjugating the original seed centrality transports it to the second span.
Both spans therefore escape the opposite kernels, and their intersections
with those kernels commute modulo the respective local Z-layers. These are
the two index comparisons preceding the FF-module assertion on printed p.902.
The spans remain the actual subgroups of the free amalgam, with a specified
conjugating element; no module classification or radius offender is assumed.

For a nonabelian first span, its derived subgroup is exactly its order-two
kernel displacement. This supplies the central commutator line needed for
the self-dual central-quotient action. Construction of that action and its
FF property remain separate from the group-theoretic results in this file.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher, Pushing up weak BN-pairs of rank two
(1993), (2.1)(vi--vii), (2.2)(iv), and (4.6.4), printed pp.855--857, 902.
-/

public section

open Subgroup Stellmacher.PushingUp.AmalgamGraph
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterC.BinaryMS.MS93.DistanceFour.Early.Containment.SpanOffender

private theorem conjugate_span_map {G : Type*} [Group G]
    (A K : Subgroup G) (f : MulAut G) :
    (⨆ g : K, A.map (MulAut.conj (g : G)).toMonoidHom).map f.toMonoidHom =
      ⨆ g : K.map f.toMonoidHom,
        (A.map f.toMonoidHom).map (MulAut.conj (g : G)).toMonoidHom := by
  have hmap (g : G) :
      (A.map (MulAut.conj g).toMonoidHom).map f.toMonoidHom =
        (A.map f.toMonoidHom).map (MulAut.conj (f g)).toMonoidHom := by
    rw [map_map, map_map]
    congr 1
    ext x
    simp
  rw [Subgroup.map_iSup]
  apply le_antisymm
  · apply iSup_le
    intro g
    rw [hmap]
    exact le_iSup_of_le
      (⟨f g, mem_map_of_mem f.toMonoidHom g.property⟩ : K.map f.toMonoidHom) le_rfl
  · apply iSup_le
    intro g
    obtain ⟨k,hk,hg⟩ := g.property
    have he : (g : G) = f k := hg.symm
    rw [he, ← hmap]
    exact le_iSup_of_le (⟨k,hk⟩ : K) le_rfl

variable {M : Type*} [Group M] [Finite M] {L R : Subgroup M}
  {source : LocalSource L R} {geometry : Geometry R}
  (common : CommonFacts R source geometry)

